  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Typhoon Julian in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration aims to mitigate the adverse effects from Typhoon Julian and displacement situations on the most vulnerable, affected communities in the Philippines. It is doing so by complementing and strengthening local capacity in responding to outstanding needs for water, sanitation and hygiene, and in accessing safer living conditions, and reduce the driving factors that could compel internally displaced persons  and their families to rely on negative coping measures to meet their basic needs during their displacement. Close coordination especially with the Department of Social Welfare and Development, the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development, the Department of Health, Batanes Disaster Risk Reduction Management Office, the Local Government Units of Batanes and other responding government leaders will be in place to maximize their response capacity and reach to the most vulnerable communities.</narrative>
  </description>
